<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		Steps to reproduce:
		1. Measure the contrast between the initials and the avatar background at
			every size, and on the iconSclass variant.

		- Expected: at least 4.5:1. Initials identify a person, so they are
			meaningful text and SC 1.4.3 applies; 18px weight 400 is below the
			large-text threshold, so the 3:1 allowance does not apply at any size.
		- Bug: avatar.less paired @colorGreyLight (#D9D9D9) with @colorGreyDark
			(#A8A8A8) for 1.68:1.

		The avatargroup overflow avatar has its own token pair and already
		passes at 6.15:1 — it is here as the control, not as a defect.
	</label>
	<hlayout spacing="16px" valign="middle">
		<avatar id="avSmall" label="AL" size="small"/>
		<avatar id="avMedium" label="GH"/>
		<avatar id="avLarge" label="KT" size="large"/>
		<avatar id="avIcon" iconSclass="z-icon-user"/>
	</hlayout>
	<avatargroup id="ag" maxCount="2">
		<avatar label="AL"/>
		<avatar label="GH"/>
		<avatar label="KT"/>
	</avatargroup>
</zk>
